article_spellcheck:
TIME AND AGAIN
On and after Monday, Oct. 31st, 1855, Passenger

Trains will run as follows, Sundays excepted;

FALL RIVER—Ar GOTH schs Maria Lunt, Boynton, New York; Madagascar, Coombs, Bangor; Mary Ann; MURPHY, Augusta.

BRISTOL—Ar 20th sch Frances Ellen, Whitman, New York.

NEWPORT—Ar 2 10th schs Chas Carroll, Ellens, Bristol for do; Counsellor, Whitmore, East Greenwich;

In port, brigs Sea Foam, Coombs from Bangor for Washington; Marshall Dutch, Coombs, do for Philadelphia; schs Lookout, Wakefield, from Portland for Baltimore; Frances Ellen, Whitman, and Nation A. Gould, from Bangor.

WICKFORD—Ar 10th sch Union, Post from New York.

HOLMES HOLE—Ar 18th, brigs Orchard, Torrey, Haskell, Baltimore or Boston; VIM Ores, Hatch, Hog Island, Md for Portsmouth; schs Mazurka, Kimball, Newport for Boston; Phoenix, Cheeter River, Md, for Bath; Alligator, Col. Inns, Philadelphia for Portsmouth; Ganges, Coombs, Fall River for Bangor; Abbie, Knight, Portland for Fortress Monroe; Nevada Mann, do for Philadelphia; Cyrus Fossett, Hodgdon, BANGOR for New York; Union, Pendleton, Rockland for do.

EDGARTOWN—Ar 18th, sch Paragon, Hatch, New York; steele, New York;

large fleet of Eastern bound vessels were in port on the 10th;

NEW BEDFORD—Ar 21st, sch Melbourne, Marsden, Elizabethport;

SALEM—Ar 21st schs Statesman, Carrolls, New York; Pinkham, Higgins, Union for Rockland; Geo Henry Wood, do for Elizabethport; Union, Williams, Bangor;

MACHIAS—Ar 18th, sch Montaine, Sawyer from New York; shall, Calais for New York.
